A||||2||Gokart||Long term parking on an angle?
Z||000000||Gokart||09-05-99||02:40 AM||||Thinking about taking my GT off the road Dec.-Mar. for the winter. I have a perfect spot for it on the side of my yard, but its a slight angle! Does it matter if the front is lower than the back or vice-versa or should I park it sideways? Would any fluids leak, etc.? TIA
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||09:41 AM||||I would park it sideways just to keep the load off the dogbone. As for leaking, it shouldn't matter. If it leaks you had a problem anyway. Move it every couple weeks anyway. weather permitting take it for a drive. leaving a car sit for months straigh can cause a number of problems.<p>Don't forget to fill the gas tank and put stabilizer in the gas and run it a few miles. This stuff helps keep the fuel from varnishing things. (StaBil or Bardahl Top Oil seem to be good) Filling the tank reduces the space that can draw in air & water durring temperature changes.
Z||000002||Gokart||09-05-99||01:11 PM||||TKS OGRE!
